    "text": {
     "en": "Winnowing separates heavy grain from light husk using wind. Sieving separates particles of different sizes, like flour from bran. Handpicking removes large unwanted pieces.\nDecantation is pouring off the clear liquid after the solid settles. Sedimentation lets heavy particles settle at the bottom.\nWe choose the method according to the properties of the mixture."
    }
